{"abstract":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder","type":"reference"},{"text":" of Snowplow’s tracker protocol, so an ","type":"text"},{"code":"HTTPDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"can send events to a Snowplow collector’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"POST \/com.snowplowanalytics.snowplow\/tp2","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"self-describing events whose schemas are the tracking plan’s.","type":"text"}],"relationshipsSections":[{"type":"conformsTo","kind":"relationships","identifiers":["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder","doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"title":"Conforms To"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SnowplowBatchEncoder","kind":"identifier"}],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"overview","type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Make the destination with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/snowplow(collector:vendor:appID:plan:backoff:clock:)","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":", which"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"fills in the endpoint, the header field that keeps the collector from setting a cookie or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"recording the request’s address, this encoder and its limits:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let snowplow = try HTTPDestination.snowplow(","    collector: collector,  \/\/ https:\/\/collector.example.com","    vendor: \"com.example\",  \/\/ your schemas' Iglu vendor","    appID: \"shop-ios\",","    plan: plan)"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The body is a self-describing JSON object of content type "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"application\/json"},{"type":"text","text":", of the schema"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"iglu:com.snowplowanalytics.snowplow\/payload_data\/jsonschema\/1-0-4"},{"type":"text","text":", whose "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"data"},{"type":"text","text":" is an array of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"events, one per record, oldest first. Every member of an event is a string, as the tracker"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"protocol has them:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"header":"row","type":"table","rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Member"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Holds"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"aid"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The app ID the encoder is made with"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"co","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The standard context’s entities (below), as the text of a self-describing JSON array of ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"contexts"},{"text":"; left out when there are none","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"dtm"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ttm"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When the event was tracked, in epoch milliseconds"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"e","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ue"},{"type":"text","text":", a self-describing event"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"eid","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The record’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"EventRecord\/id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", as a lowercase UUID; a redelivered record keeps it","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ip"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0.0.0.0"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"p","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The platform: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"mob"},{"type":"text","text":" for a phone, pad, watch or Vision Pro, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tv"},{"type":"text","text":" for an Apple TV, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"pc"},{"type":"text","text":" for a Mac, and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"app"},{"type":"text","text":" when the record has no device in its context"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"sid"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The record’s session, its ","type":"text"},{"code":"SessionKey","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", as a lowercase UUID; left out when its context has no session","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tv"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"traffluent","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", the tracker"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ue_pr"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The event, as the text of a self-describing JSON ","type":"text"},{"code":"unstruct_event","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" holding the event’s own self-describing JSON: its schema, ","type":"text"},{"code":"iglu:<vendor>\/<name>\/jsonschema\/<version>-0-0","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and its data, its stored properties by name","type":"text"}]}]]]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The session is the only identifier sent: there is no "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"duid"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"uid"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nuid"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tnuid"},{"type":"text","text":", no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"client_session"},{"type":"text","text":" entity, whose "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"userId"},{"type":"text","text":" lasts across sessions, and no "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"appleIdfv"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"appleIdfa"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"or other device identifier. Snowplow’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"domain_sessionid"},{"type":"text","text":" is the session; a record with no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"session (one tracked by a tracker without "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Enricher.sessions()"},{"type":"text","text":") is sent without one, linked to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"nothing. A record a store recovers after a relaunch keeps its session, so it goes out with the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"sid"},{"type":"text","text":" of its first send. The record’s vendor"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"identifier and trace context, and any other context value, aren’t sent."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Each event’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"ttm","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", its true timestamp, is the record’s timestamp, as is ","type":"text"},{"code":"dtm","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so Snowplow’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"derived_tstamp","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is when the event was tracked, uncorrected for the device’s clock. No ","type":"text"},{"code":"stm","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is sent: a retried request sends the same body again, so a sent time would be the first","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"attempt’s, and Snowplow would move the event later by however long the retries took.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The event’s schema is named after its ","type":"text"},{"code":"Event\/name","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"Event\/schemaVersion","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":": version N is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"SchemaVer ","type":"text"},{"code":"N-0-0","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Each version of an event is a breaking change, a SchemaVer MODEL. A","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"compatible change at the same version is an ADDITION, which the tracking plan’s Iglu export","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"code":"TrackingPlan\/writeIgluRegistry(to:vendor:registry:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") writes for Iglu Server as ","type":"text"},{"code":"N-0-1","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"on, each superseding the ones before, so an event naming ","type":"text"},{"code":"N-0-0","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is validated against the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"newest of them. A static repository doesn’t supersede: there an event naming ","type":"text"},{"code":"N-0-0","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"validated against ","type":"text"},{"code":"N-0-0","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" alone, so the export refuses an addition for one, and a change to an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"event needs a new version.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Properties are read through the event’s schema in "},{"code":"plan","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", as "},{"code":"PropertyReader","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" reads them. A"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/Sensitive","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" value is never sent, whatever the record reveals: the property is left"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"out, an element of an array is "},{"code":"null","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and one inside a type the plan can’t map is "},{"code":"null","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". The"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"data then validates against the event’s exported schema, which never requires a "},{"code":"Sensitive","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"property."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"co","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" holds these entities, for the keys the record’s context has values for:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"header":"row","type":"table","rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Entity"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Keys","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Holds"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"iglu:com.snowplowanalytics.snowplow\/mobile_context\/jsonschema\/1-0-3","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"DeviceKey","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"OperatingSystemKey","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", both; "},{"code":"NetworkKey","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"LocaleKey","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" if present"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"osType","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" ("},{"code":"ios","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"tvos","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"watchos","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"visionos","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"osx","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"), "},{"code":"osVersion","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"deviceManufacturer","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" ("},{"code":"Apple Inc.","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"), "},{"code":"deviceModel","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"; "},{"code":"networkType","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" ("},{"code":"wifi","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"mobile","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"offline","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"; left out for a wired or other connection); "},{"code":"language","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", the locale’s language code"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"iglu:com.snowplowanalytics.mobile\/application\/jsonschema\/1-0-0","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"ApplicationKey","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", with both a version and a build"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"version"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"build"}]}]]]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A record the encoder can’t write is left out of the request, and the batch’s other records are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sent: one whose event and version "},{"code":"plan","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" doesn’t describe, one whose event name Iglu doesn’t"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"take, one whose event isn’t "},{"code":"Encodable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", one that holds a value JSON can’t, one whose timestamp"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is outside the years 0 to 9999, and one whose JSON is over 150,000 bytes"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/SnowplowEncodingError","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":")."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/SnowplowBatchEncoder\/requests(for:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" returns them as "},{"code":"SkippedRecord","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"s, which "},{"code":"HTTPDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" logs and reports"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"on its "},{"code":"dropReports","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/SnowplowBatchEncoder\/requests(for:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" splits a batch into requests within the encoder’s limit, "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/SnowplowBatchEncoder\/batchLimit","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"default, and makes none for a batch with no record it can write, so "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"type":"text","text":" sends"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"nothing for it. The collector answers 200 to every request it can read, and Snowplow validates"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the events afterwards: an event whose data its schema rejects, or whose schema the pipeline’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Iglu resolver can’t find, becomes a failed event, kept apart from the warehouse, though the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"destination counts it as delivered. The bytes are the same for the same records on every run"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and platform: no whitespace, object members in the order of their names’ UTF-8 bytes."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"topicSections":[{"generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/SnowplowBatchEncoder\/init(vendor:appID:plan:limit:)"],"anchor":"Initializers","title":"Init